		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=34026#p34026"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>I am trying to create a user mapping in PostgreSQL without a password, but I am encountering an error that says </p><p>local_db=&gt; select * from employee;<br />ERROR:&#160; could not connect to server &quot;testmachine02&quot;<br />DETAIL:&#160; connection to server at &quot;192.168.56.10&quot;, port 5432 failed: fe_sendauth: no password supplied<br />local_db=&gt; exit </p><p> when I try to access a table. Here is the command that I used to create the user mapping:</p><p>CREATE USER MAPPING for app_user SERVER testmachine02 OPTIONS (password_required &#039;false&#039;);</p><br /><p>I also created a pgpass under /root/.pgpass file with the following entries:</p><p>localhost:5432:local_db:app_user:app_user123<br />192.168.56.10:5432:admin:admin:admin123<br />192.168.56.10:5432:remote_db:test:test123<br />testmachine02:5432:remote_db:test:test123</p><p>Despite these steps, I am still unable to access the table without a password. How can I create a user mapping without a password and access the table?</p>]]></content>
